Alembic revisions for mecha-api.

    pnpm --filter api migrate:new "add users"   # diff tables.py → revision
    pnpm --filter api migrate                   # alembic upgrade head

env.py reads MECHA_DATABASE_URL through the app's settings, so no URL lives
in alembic.ini. Autogenerated revisions are a starting point, not an answer.
Read them before committing, and replace any `mecha_api.*` type reference
with the plain SQLAlchemy type it wraps so old revisions survive refactors.

The app runs `upgrade head` at startup unless MECHA_MIGRATE_ON_STARTUP=false.
`test_store.py` fails if tables.py and these revisions ever disagree.
